      "index": 119,
      "start": 418.8,
      "end": 422.55,
      "duration": 3.75,
      "text": "each fixed omega the output is going to"
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": 422.56,
      "end": 425.189,
      "duration": 2.629,
      "text": "be a sinosoid which oscillates at the"
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": 425.199,
      "end": 427.43,
      "duration": 2.231,
      "text": "same frequency as the input. However the"
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": 427.44,
      "end": 429.27,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "only difference is that it's going to"
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": 429.28,
      "end": 431.11,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "res it's going to have a rescaled"
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": 431.12,
      "end": 433.83,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "amplitude and it'll have a shifted phase"
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": 433.84,
      "end": 436.309,
      "duration": 2.469,
      "text": "as well."
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "start": 436.319,
      "end": 440.95,
      "duration": 4.631,
      "text": "So for the amplitude response,"
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "start": 443.83,
      "end": 443.84,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "we're interested in plotting one over"
    },
    {
      "index": 128,
      "start": 443.84,
      "end": 446.71,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "the amplitude of P of I omega."
    },
    {
      "index": 129,
      "start": 446.72,
      "end": 455.51,
      "duration": 8.79,
      "text": "So here's the amplitude"
    },
    {
      "index": 130,
      "start": 456.95,
      "end": 456.96,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "and this function is just going to"
    },
    {
      "index": 131,
      "start": 456.96,
      "end": 459.749,
      "duration": 2.789,
      "text": "decrease and asmtoically approach"
    },
    {
      "index": 132,
      "start": 459.759,
      "end": 461.83,
      "duration": 2.071,
      "text": "infinity."
    },
    {
      "index": 133,
      "start": 461.84,
      "end": 464.23,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "Okay, so this is the amplitude response."
    },
    {
      "index": 134,
      "start": 464.24,
      "end": 468.55,
      "duration": 4.31,
      "text": "This is 1 7 - omega^ 2<unk>"
    },
    {
      "index": 135,
      "start": 468.56,
      "end": 471.029,
      "duration": 2.469,
      "text": "+ 8 omega^"
    },
    {
      "index": 136,
      "start": 471.039,
      "end": 474.07,
      "duration": 3.031,
      "text": "2 rooted."
    },
    {
      "index": 137,
      "start": 474.08,
      "end": 477.99,
      "duration": 3.91,
      "text": "This is omega."
    },
    {
      "index": 138,
      "start": 479.589,
      "end": 479.599,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And then in addition to the amplitude"
    },
    {
      "index": 139,
      "start": 479.599,
      "end": 485.27,
      "duration": 5.671,
      "text": "response, we also have the phase."
    },
    {
      "index": 140,
      "start": 487.83,
      "end": 487.84,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Okay. And the phase, if I go back up"
    },
    {
      "index": 141,
      "start": 487.84,
      "end": 490.07,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "here for a second, we can write it"
    },
    {
      "index": 142,
      "start": 490.08,
      "end": 492.309,
      "duration": 2.229,
      "text": "explicitly as phi is equal to tan"
    },
    {
      "index": 143,
      "start": 492.319,
      "end": 496.469,
      "duration": 4.15,
      "text": "inverse"
    },
    {
      "index": 144,
      "start": 498.39,
      "end": 498.4,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "8 omega"
    },
    {
      "index": 145,
      "start": 498.4,
      "end": 503.11,
      "duration": 4.71,
      "text": "/ 7 - omega^ 2."
    },
    {
      "index": 146,
      "start": 506.39,
      "end": 506.4,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So I'm going to plot omega on this axis"
    },
    {
      "index": 147,
      "start": 506.4,
      "end": 509.27,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "and phi on this axis."
    },
    {
      "index": 148,
      "start": 509.28,
      "end": 512.79,
      "duration": 3.51,
      "text": "And okay, so to plot this curve, we note"
    },
    {
      "index": 149,
      "start": 512.8,
      "end": 515.909,
      "duration": 3.109,
      "text": "that when omega is zero,"
    },
    {
      "index": 150,
      "start": 515.919,
      "end": 518.949,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "uh tan inverse of 0 is zero. So we're"
    },
    {
      "index": 151,
      "start": 518.959,
      "end": 521.029,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "going to start at zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 152,
      "start": 521.039,
      "end": 523.67,
      "duration": 2.631,
      "text": "Um,"
    },
    {
      "index": 153,
      "start": 523.68,
      "end": 525.43,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "typically what I usually like to do in"
    },
    {
      "index": 154,
      "start": 525.44,
      "end": 527.67,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "this case is look at the denominator in"
    },
    {
      "index": 155,
      "start": 527.68,
      "end": 529.99,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "the arc tangent. We see that when omega"
    },
    {
      "index": 156,
      "start": 530.0,
      "end": 532.47,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "is equal to the<unk> of 7, this argument"
    },
    {
      "index": 157,
      "start": 532.48,
      "end": 535.11,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "blows up. It goes to infinity. And the"
    },
    {
      "index": 158,
      "start": 535.12,
      "end": 539.43,
      "duration": 4.31,
      "text": "arc tangent of infinity is pi / 2. So I"
    },
    {
      "index": 159,
      "start": 539.44,
      "end": 542.47,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "can draw a curve in here which is pi /"
    },
    {
      "index": 160,
      "start": 542.48,
      "end": 545.829,
      "duration": 3.349,
      "text": "2."
    },
    {
      "index": 161,
      "start": 548.47,
      "end": 548.48,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So we know that phi is pi / 2 when omega"
    },
    {
      "index": 162,
      "start": 548.48,
      "end": 550.79,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "is equal to roo<unk> 7. And note how"
    },
    {
      "index": 163,
      "start": 550.8,
      "end": 554.949,
      "duration": 4.149,
      "text": "this is the uh the the natural frequency"
    },
    {
      "index": 164,
      "start": 554.959,
      "end": 559.75,
      "duration": 4.791,
      "text": "if there was no damping in the system."
    },
    {
      "index": 165,
      "start": 561.19,
      "end": 561.2,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And then lastly there's another curve"
    },
    {
      "index": 166,
      "start": 561.2,
      "end": 563.19,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "here at pi."
    },
    {
      "index": 167,
      "start": 563.2,
      "end": 566.07,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "We see that as omega approaches infinity"
    },
    {
      "index": 168,
      "start": 566.08,
      "end": 572.949,
      "duration": 6.869,
      "text": "again this argument uh approaches zero."
    },
    {
      "index": 169,
      "start": 574.55,
      "end": 574.56,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And if if you were to take the"
    },
    {
      "index": 170,
      "start": 574.56,
      "end": 576.63,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "derivative of this whole quantity, we"
    },
    {
      "index": 171,
      "start": 576.64,
      "end": 580.55,
      "duration": 3.91,
      "text": "would see that uh it's uh of tan inverse"
    },
    {
      "index": 172,
      "start": 580.56,
      "end": 582.23,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "of this argument, we would see that the"
    },
    {
      "index": 173,
      "start": 582.24,
      "end": 585.11,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "functions increasing for all omega. So"
    },
    {
      "index": 174,
      "start": 585.12,
      "end": 588.79,
      "duration": 3.67,
      "text": "it actually looks something like this."
    },
    {
      "index": 175,
      "start": 588.8,
      "end": 591.03,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "It looks like an S-shaped curve that"
    },
    {
      "index": 176,
      "start": 591.04,
      "end": 593.67,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "asmtoically approaches pi as omega goes"
    },
    {
      "index": 177,
      "start": 593.68,
      "end": 596.15,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "to infinity."
    },
    {
      "index": 178,
      "start": 596.16,
      "end": 598.63,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "Okay, so just to quickly recap when we"
    },
    {
      "index": 179,
      "start": 598.64,
      "end": 601.91,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "look at uh the differential equation uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 180,
      "start": 601.92,
      "end": 603.43,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "or a particular solution to a"
    },
    {
      "index": 181,
      "start": 603.44,
      "end": 604.63,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "differential equation which is being"
    },
    {
      "index": 182,
      "start": 604.64,
      "end": 607.43,
      "duration": 2.79,
      "text": "forced by a periodic sinosoidal"
    },
    {
      "index": 183,
      "start": 607.44,
      "end": 609.11,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "function,"
    },
    {
      "index": 184,
      "start": 609.12,
      "end": 611.509,
      "duration": 2.389,
      "text": "the output is always going to be"
    },
    {
      "index": 185,
      "start": 611.519,
      "end": 614.389,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "rescaled and phase shifted but still"
    },
    {
      "index": 186,
      "start": 614.399,
      "end": 617.35,
      "duration": 2.951,
      "text": "oscillating at the same frequency."
    },
    {
      "index": 187,
      "start": 617.36,
      "end": 619.269,
      "duration": 1.909,
      "text": "And specifically depending on which"
    },
    {
      "index": 188,
      "start": 619.279,
      "end": 620.79,
      "duration": 1.511,
      "text": "frequency"
    },
    {
      "index": 189,
      "start": 620.8,
      "end": 622.389,
      "duration": 1.589,
      "text": "uh the differential equation is forced"
    },
    {
      "index": 190,
      "start": 622.399,
      "end": 625.829,
      "duration": 3.43,
      "text": "at the amplitude will take on different"
    },
    {
      "index": 191,
      "start": 625.839,
      "end": 627.67,
      "duration": 1.831,
      "text": "values. The amplitude response will take"
    },
    {
      "index": 192,
      "start": 627.68,
      "end": 630.55,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "on different values and the phase shift"
    },
    {
      "index": 193,
      "start": 630.56,
      "end": 632.389,
      "duration": 1.829,
      "text": "will also have different values"
    },
    {
      "index": 194,
      "start": 632.399,
      "end": 635.19,
      "duration": 2.791,
      "text": "depending on the frequency of forcing."
    },
    {
      "index": 195,
      "start": 635.2,
      "end": 636.87,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "Okay. So I'd just like to conclude here"
    },
    {
      "index": 196,
      "start": 636.88,
      "end": 640.56,
      "duration": 3.68,
      "text": "and I'll see you next time."
    }
